  "id": "DrugBank_DB00811 - MONDO_5231",
  "verbalization": "Ribavirin is associated with the treatment of Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection through a series of indirect pathways, as evidenced by its indication in combination with other antiviral agents. The evidence suggests that Ribavirin may exert a role in the management of Hepatitis C Virus Infection by influencing the host's immune response or by interacting with viral proteins, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple indications for Ribavirin in the context of Hepatitis C Virus Infection, along with its association with drugs like Vaniprevir, Simeprevir, and Velpatasvir, indicates a potential role in the treatment of the disease. These drugs are all antiviral agents that target the Hepatitis C Virus, and their shared indication with Ribavirin suggests a possible synergistic or complementary effect. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Ribavirin may contribute to the antiviral activity of these drugs, though further mechanistic studies are needed to elucidate the precise mechanism of action.",
